Z||000000||FIEROCIOUS||03-30-2000||11:48 PM||||I just recieved my coil-overs from Ryane Motorsports! They are of excellent quality! I (being the picky A-hole I am) am very pleased!<P>Batboy, What size tire do you think will fit with the coil-overs?<BR>305? J/K<P>I would like to use 15 or 16 inch tires. I have the baretta brake upgrade and the back spaceing is different now because of the rotor thickness! +7mm front +3mm rear. Stock backspaceing is 35mm.<P>Anyone have an idea what back spaceing I should use now? What back spaceing with the coil-overs?<P>Thanks In advance!||||reg||1
Z||000001||phillip||03-31-2000||12:21 PM||||don't know about the brake change. on a stock '87 coupe i have 16X7.5 wheels with a 35mm pos. offset. i was using 225/50 16's on the back but am switching to 255/50 16s for the rear. on my wheel the edge of the rim barely misses the lower strut mounting point. i am getting coilovers too eventualy to fit the new tires but since the strut mounting point is the same the wheels themselves will have the same clearance.<BR>dose any one remember the fiero in hot rod (oct. '87)? pontiac made some pieces that set the struts inboard for more wheel clearance.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIEROCIOUS||04-01-2000||01:36 AM||||Batboy? Where are you man? <P>I've looked at my tire options and the pickins are slim! If I go with a 265/50-15<BR>only one brand makes them (BFG) and no one makes a 265/40-16! I'd like to keep the radius close to stock. 17 are too darn heavy! ||||reg||1
