Z||000004||batboy||04-01-2000||08:58 AM||||Hey Fierocious, I'm in the same exact boat as you. I have to find some wheels and tires. Unfortunately (or luckily depending on your point of view) I just spent my budgeted wheel and tire money on a freshly built 454 for my 72 Chevy pickup. But, I had decided if I found a good set of used 15" wheels, I'd run BFG Comp T/A 255/60ZR15 in the rear. If I buy new wheels, it'll be 16" ones and I'll mount Comp T/A 255/50ZR16. Either should fit good with coil-overs. That size is a good compromise between looks and handling.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 04-01-2000).]||||reg||1
